<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Czechoslovak National Council</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1916–1918</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Czechoslovak National Council was the organisation of the Czech and Slovak independence movement abroad, founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1916 with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tomas-garrigue-masaryk">Tomáš Garrigue Masaryk</a> as chairman, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edvard-benes">Edvard Beneš</a> as secretary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan-rastislav-stefanik">Milan Rastislav Štefánik</a>. Supported by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-legion">Czechoslovak Legions</a>, it won recognition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> in 1918 and became the provisional government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/czechoslovak-national-council.jpg" alt="Czechoslovak National Council" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Milan Rastislav Štefánik · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Czechoslovak_National_Council.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
